        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00058",
          "explanation": "Doctor explains that 30-plus mmol/L/HI indicates very high blood sugar, not low.",
          "quote": "口渴是高血糖比较常见的表现，不用刻意限制老人喝水"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00717",
          "explanation": "Caregiver acknowledges the corrected high-versus-low distinction and repeats the plan.",
          "quote": "我现在记的是：如果已经打了但不吃了，就赶紧给1-2块糖或者半杯糖水"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO1 is triggered when the family says 'HI' or '三十多' in a context implying possible low glucose; the doctor subsequently explains in plain language that these values indicate severe hyperglycemia while also validating that insulin therapy creates a real hypoglycemia risk. The caregiver’s teach-back confirms the corrected distinction.",
      "ho_id": "HO1",
