          "quote": "出院前才会把以后是不是改成皮下注射、带不带口服降糖药或胰岛素、具体打多少、什么时候复诊，都写到出院医嘱或出院小结里"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO2 is triggered because the family’s opening account is incomplete; the doctor uses targeted questions and multiple workspace queries to uncover numerous non-volunteered action-relevant facts (repeated HI/30-plus capillary glucose, insulin IV pump, q2h monitoring, endocrine urgent consultation, TIA history, fall/wandering precautions) and integrates them into the risk framing and handoff plan.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [],
      "completion": "not_triggered",
      "explanation": "HO3 is not triggered because the family never states that symptoms alone are sufficient to distinguish high from low glucose, nor that a measured glucose value is unnecessary. The doctor’s red-flag screening and advice to measure glucose before acting are already required by RC2 and RC3, and no conditional pathway beyond those minimum responsibilities is required.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00079",
          "explanation": "Doctor provides a written checklist-like plan for the next 24–72 hours, including glucose log, medication boundaries, and fall precautions.",
          "quote": "回家血糖记录本怎么记：每次测血糖后，只需要记3项：日期、时间（比如“早餐前”“睡前”）、血糖数值就行"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00746",
          "explanation": "Doctor specifies what to record, what questions to ask, and adds practical safety steps.",
          "quote": "如果老人夜里突然变得特别嗜睡、喊他反应比平时慢，也可能是低血糖的不典型表现"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00337",
          "explanation": "Caregiver confirms the checklist is feasible and addresses remaining barriers.",
          "quote": "我现在就按出院处方给他打晚饭前这一针，不加量、不补针，然后守着他吃粥"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO4 is triggered when the family reports confusion about monitoring frequency and insulin use, and the doctor creates a practical 24–72-hour execution plan with glucose/symptom log, concrete questions for the clinical team, and fall-prevention steps. The caregiver confirms the plan is feasible and explicitly acknowledges the corrected boundaries.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    }
  ],
